              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for every day, then the Marathi for summer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: हिवाळा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हिवाळा — hivāḷā — \"winter\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हिवाळा (hivāḷā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from himakāla, \"winter-time\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 14098). It is hima, \"cold, snow\", and kāla, \"time\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
